  "alternatives": [],
  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of Alaska Medicaid CGRP receptor antagonists oral and injectable, Version 2. Original 10/12/2018; Approval 09/18/2020; Updated 09/19/2025; Effective 11/1/2025.",
    "Closed prevention indication covers episodic or chronic migraine diagnosis and use for prophylaxis (prevention approval criteria 3 and 5), with an injectable or oral agent labeled for prevention. Closed acute indication covers migraine with or without aura and an oral agent labeled for acute treatment.",
    "Age is an attestation to the individual agent FDA label; no single numeric age threshold is imposed on the class.",
    "Prior prophylactic therapy examples include beta blockers, antiepileptics and antidepressants. The source requires trials, not a separately documented failure or intolerance; fact keys retain the failed naming convention.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval up to 3 months; reauthorization up to 12 months. Quantity limit (notes only): 34 days.",
    "Cautions: injection site reactions are common with injectables. Strong CYP3A4 inhibitors are contraindicated with oral CGRPs; this is also encoded on the acute path. For oral prevention, this caution requires manual review.",
    "Remains partial: individual FDA labeling, evidence verification, duration, reauthorization, quantity and cautions require manual review."
  ],
